int write = 0;

for (int read = 1; read < n; read++) {
  if (intervals[read].start < intervals[write].end) {
    if (intervals[read].end > intervals[write].end) {
      // Extend current interval
      intervals[write].end = intervals[read].end;
    }
  } else {
    // Start a new interval
    intervals[++write] = intervals[read];
  }
}
```

Note: use `intervals[read].start <= intervals[write].end` if touching counts as overlap.

